// ============================================================
// presentation/slides.json -- every word on the /present slides.
//
// Edit wording here; no code changes needed. Save the file and
// refresh /present in the browser: the page reads this file each
// time it opens, so Isa does NOT need a restart (and must not be
// restarted mid-talk: ticket numbers would start again at TKT-0001).
//
// Rules for the wording (Isa_Presentation_Breakdown.md):
// - The Client is never named on a slide.
// - No model timing on the slides.
// - Keep dev-only items (test scripts, the launcher) off the slides.
//
// Each slide has a "kind" that decides its layout:
//   landing, cover, problem, statement, rules, safetynet, pipeline, status, showwork, list,
//   demo, numbered, features, closing.
// "presenter" shows in the corner, so hand-offs are clear.
// In "lead", a word between *asterisks* is shown in italics and colour.
// On a "problem" slide, \n in "lead" starts a new line.
// Lines starting with // are comments and are ignored.
// ============================================================
